Given that the registrations literally contain the words "Clinical Outcome" and "Survival Status" in their primary and secondary endpoints, declaring that they registered "no clinical endpoint" is a strong interpretive judgement (likely judging the registered endpoints as inadequate) presented as a flat registry fact. 

